# Author Kit - Claude Code Instructions

You are an AI writing assistant working within the Author Kit framework.

## Project Structure

- `.authorkit/memory/constitution.md` - Style bible (voice/tone/style rules)
- `.authorkit/templates/` - Canonical templates for every file Author Kit writes
- `{{SCRIPT_DIR}}` - Automation scripts
- `book/` - Book workspace (concept, outline, chapters, world, research, parked decisions, amendments, snapshots)

## Workflow

Author Kit exposes **four slash commands** under `{{COMMAND_SOURCE}}`. They map to authoring activities, not to artifacts. The model handles all scaffolding (concept.md, outline.md, world/, chapters.md, parked-decisions.md, characters.md, constitution, snapshots, amendments) as side-effects.

- **`/authorkit.discuss`** — talk through anything: brainstorm an idea, clarify ambiguities, decide and route the answer to the right file, propagate a cross-cutting change with an impact plan, restructure chapters, try a what-if on an experimental branch, update voice/tone rules, defer a question, save discussion notes. Read-only by default; every write is proposed and confirmed before it happens. Use this for the very first session on an empty repo too — it produces `concept.md`.
- **`/authorkit.write`** — produce manuscript prose. Generates `outline.md` and `chapters.md` when missing, plans the requested chapter, drafts it (full pass or scene-by-scene / continue / from-scene / interactive), revises an existing draft, helps with a specific passage, and reconciles state after writing (extracts new world details, refreshes outline summary, updates `chapters.md` status, scans for new ambiguities, rebuilds `world/_index.md`).
- **`/authorkit.review`** — review one chapter (craft-level: plan adherence, constitution compliance, craft quality, character/world consistency, continuity, theme integration; produces `chapters/NN/review.md`) or the whole manuscript (drift, continuity, threads, pacing, voice, world-building, overdue parked decisions; read-only with gated upstream drift fixes). A range argument runs both.
- **`/authorkit.research`** — grounded research for a topic from web/news/wikipedia/MCP sources. Writes a topic file under `research/` and updates `research.md`. Offers world sync when findings are durable and clearly map to a `world/` category, gated by chat-level approval.

## State the model manages (do not ask the author to edit these by hand)

- `book/concept.md` — premise, audience, voice, themes, scope, success criteria, Clarifications log
- `book/outline.md` — structural overview, chapter breakdowns, character arcs, thematic threads, Continuation Notes for partial outlines
- `book/chapters.md` — chapter status list (`[ ]` pending, `[P]` planned, `[D]` drafted, `[R]` reviewed-needs-work, `[X]` approved)
- `book/characters.md` — index of character profiles
- `book/world/` — characters/, places/, organizations/, history/, systems/, notes/ with YAML frontmatter and `(CONCEPT)`/`(CHxx)`/`(CHxx-rev)`/`(AMEND-…)` tags
- `book/world/_index.md` — generated entity registry, alias lookup, chapter manifest (rebuilt after world writes)
- `book/research.md`, `book/research/**/*.md` — grounded research index and topic notes
- `book/parked-decisions.md` — deferred decisions with deadlines (`Before CHNN` / `Before final draft` / `No deadline`)
- `book/chapters/NN/{plan.md, draft.md, review.md}` — per-chapter plan, prose draft, craft review
- `book/style-anchor.md` — prose continuity anchor (constitution + concept voice/tone + earliest approved chapters, the fixed origin), refreshed before drafting/revising
- `book/snapshots/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md` — narrative bookmarks (paired with `snapshot/*` git tags) created before risky operations
- `book/amendments/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md` — change logs for cross-cutting amendments
- `book/whatif-active.md` — present only while a what-if experimental branch is in flight
- `book/notes/discuss-*.md` — discussion notes saved on author request

## Notes

- Use absolute paths when operating on files.
- World files use YAML frontmatter; rebuild `world/_index.md` after any world write (the `/authorkit.write` reconcile pass and `/authorkit.discuss` mode that touches `world/` both do this automatically).
- Style continuity anchors to `.authorkit/memory/constitution.md` + concept voice/tone + `book/style-anchor.md` + the earliest approved chapter drafts (`[X]`, the fixed origin) when available; character/scene *texture* matches the earliest *relevant* approved chapter (never a trailing one).
- Prefer original, distinctive character/place names; avoid repeated stock-name patterns and generic defaults.
- Numeric facts in new prose need rationale; when multiple values are plausible, pick a context-bounded varied value, not a repetitive default.
- Handoff `prompt:` strings may contain bracketed placeholders such as `[N]` (chapter), `[topic]`, `[focus area]`. When forwarding a handoff, substitute the relevant value from the conversation context — never forward the literal bracketed text.
- Every command ends its turn with a list of files written (paths + one-line summary). If nothing was written, say so.
